		</element>
		<!-- Fn and Win both need to fire the Fn+Win hard-reset chord (see fn_win_reset() in
		     homecomputer6502.cpp) from a single click. A clickable item only fires if its
		     inputmask exactly matches one ioport_field's mask (see render.cpp
		     render_target::update_pointer_fields()/pointer_updated(): port->field(mask) is an
		     exact-match lookup), and RESET has two separate 1-bit fields (0x01 and 0x02) - no
		     field has mask 0x03 - so each keycap needs two stacked overlays, one per bit,
		     rather than a single item with the combined mask.
		     clickthrough="yes" is required on both: an item with an inputtag defaults to
		     clickthrough="no" (see resolve_tags()), which makes it "obscure" the pointer for
		     any item stacked underneath (render.cpp update_pointer_fields(): the topmost hit
		     item sets a per-pointer "obscured" bit that suppresses hits on lower items) - so
		     without this, only the topmost of each stacked pair would ever actually fire. -->
